# A book's whole description, with the panel to itself. The book's own screen
# has room for a taste of it, the blurb is reached by tapping that, it pages with
# the same two buttons every list here uses, and Back is the book rather than the
# list the book was found in.
clean
tap Recent releases
wait-for Filters
tap Mensonges
wait-for Book details
expect Marilou Addison
expect 312 pages
expect About this book
expect Un été de trop
clean
tap Un été de trop
wait-for About this book
expect Un été de trop
expect Page 1 of
expect Previous page
expect Next page
clean
tap Next page
wait-for Page 2
expect-missing Un été de trop
clean
tap Previous page
wait-for Page 1
expect Un été de trop
clean
tap Back
wait-for Book details
expect Choose a library
clean
# Back first returns to the browse list, then to the section index.
tap Back
wait-for Filters
tap Back
wait-for Prêt numérique
# How much of a book there is is one fact, and it is whichever of the two the
# catalogue counted: an audiobook is hours, and has no pages at all.
tap Next page
wait-for Littérature queer
tap Littérature queer
wait-for Filters
tap Le Somnambule
wait-for Book details
expect 9 h 12 min
expect-missing pages
clean
# And the one title nobody counted draws nothing where the count would be,
# rather than a row with nothing in it.
tap Back
wait-for Filters
tap Typiquement Eliza
wait-for Book details
expect Sophie Lee
expect-missing Length
clean
